35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The receipts show we spend 2,300 yen monthly on duplicates. The management office charges 4,200 yen per hour for contracted help.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The stopwatch run totaled one hundred and two minutes. The firm’s terms require someone present to tidy beforehand, so the time burden isn’t fully removed.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The calendar shows two of us away weekly, and one was gone all August. Yet the kitchen watch shows only two or three of us actually cooking.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"My findings show we define ""done"" differently, causing the state to swing. The chat logs reveal our rows start with reminders about undone tasks.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The previous tenants divided rooms permanently, but by year two, two of them barely spoke. The chat logs confirm our rows start with reminders.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Midori"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Midori: The previous tenants divided rooms permanently, but by year two, two of them barely spoke. The chat logs confirm our rows start with reminders.""}]}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, if the firm needs us present, does that just shift the burden rather than remove it?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"It shifts it. We still need to tidy beforehand, so the prep time remains. It doesn’t remove the burden, just changes who does the heavy lifting.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the 4,200 yen rate is steep. If we hire them, we need to know exactly who settles that invoice monthly.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, that’s a fair point. But the real issue is that we don’t agree on what “done” even means, so the invoice is the least of our worries.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I agree. The previous tenants’ silence proves that rigid division breeds resentment. We need a system that prevents those reminders from becoming arguments.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, the office bill goes to one named tenant who collects from the rest. I need to know if that collection process is reliable or if it creates debt.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, that collection risk is real. But my stopwatch data shows the prep work alone is significant. We can’t outsource the time we don’t have.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, that collection risk is real. But my data shows the work is uneven. If we hire, we must ensure the bill doesn’t just land on whoever is home that day.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Midori, the reminders are the trigger. If we define ""done"" clearly, we stop the cycle before it starts.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@May, exactly. If we agree on the standard, the reminders disappear. I’d rather we define ""done"" together than let it drift into resentment again.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
